## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| 🔴 Critical | 2 (one systemic, covering all 10 tests) |
| 🟡 Medium | 2 |
| ⚪ Low | 1 |

**This suite is the textbook case you described.** Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called (→ 95% coverage), but virtually nothing is verified. All 10 tests will pass even if the production code is completely broken.

---

### 🔴 Critical

#### 1. Coverage-Touching Suite (systemic — all 10 tests)

The class methodically calls every public method on `ProductCatalog` in declaration order with no meaningful assertions. **6 of 10 tests have zero assertions; the other 4 use only `Assert.IsNotNull`**, which proves a non-null reference was returned but never that the *correct value* was returned.

| Test Method | Lines | Assertion | What It Misses |
|---|---|---|---|
| `AddProduct_Works` | 17–21 | ❌ None | Never checks the product was actually stored |
| `GetProduct_Works` | 23–29 | `IsNotNull` | Never checks Sku/Name/Price match |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` | 31–36 | ❌ None | Never checks price actually changed |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` | 38–43 | ❌ None | Never checks product is gone |
| `SearchProducts_Works` | 45–52 | `IsNotNull` | Never checks results contain "Widget" or correct count |
| `GetAllProducts_Works` | 54–60 | `IsNotNull` | Never checks count or contents |
| `GetProductCount_Works` | 63–66 | ❌ None | Never checks count == 0 |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | 68–74 | ❌ None | Never checks prices were reduced |
| `ExportToCsv_Works` | 76–82 | `IsNotNull` | Never checks CSV content |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` | 85–88 | ❌ None | Never checks product was imported |

**Concrete fixes** (showing before → after for each):

```csharp
// AddProduct_Works → AddProduct_StoresProduct
var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var stored = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(stored);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", stored.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, stored.Price);
```

```csharp
// GetProduct_Works → GetProduct_ReturnsCorrectProduct
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
var result = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(result);
Assert.AreEqual("SKU-001", result.Sku);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", result.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, result.Price);
```

```csharp
